  m_Name: L24_Ayasofya
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Cutrium.Presentation::Cutrium.Presentation.Landmark.LandmarkDefinition
  _landmarkId: ayasofya
  _displayTitle: Hagia Sophia
  _shortDescription: Completed in 537, Hagia Sophia's immense dome was a turning
    point in architectural history. Used over the centuries as a church, mosque,
    and museum, the building brings Byzantine and Ottoman heritage together in one
    space. The pendentives connecting the dome to the square main hall were a major
    engineering innovation, while mosaics and monumental calligraphic roundels make
    its different eras visible side by side.
  _sector: Istanbul / TURKEY
  _displayTitleTurkish: Ayasofya
  _shortDescriptionTurkish: "537\u2019de tamamlanan Ayasofya\u2019n\u0131n dev kubbesi,
    mimarl\u0131k tarihinde bir d\xF6n\xFCm noktas\u0131yd\u0131. Y\xFCzy\u0131llar
    boyunca kilise, cami ve m\xFCze olarak kullan\u0131lan yap\u0131, Bizans ve Osmanl\u0131
    miras\u0131n\u0131 ayn\u0131 mek\xE2nda bulu\u015Fturur. Kubbeyi kare ana mek\xE2na
    ba\u011Flayan pandantifler b\xFCy\xFCk bir m\xFChendislik yenili\u011Fiydi; mozaikler
    ile dev hat levhalar\u0131 da farkl\u0131 d\xF6nemleri yan yana g\xF6r\xFCn\xFCr
    k\u0131lar."
  _sectorTurkish: "\u0130stanbul / T\xDCRK\u0130YE"
  _artwork: {fileID: -8581728456637405341, guid: 31fad58d54e36e1458b54f587f804ca4, type: 3}
